Z||000005||Formula88||08-16-2001||10:15 PM||||I find it interesting that more and more celebrities are being "found out" as gay after their deaths.  To believe all of them would mean a lot of actors were gay.<P>Cary Grant<BR>Clark Gable<BR>John Wayne<BR>James Dean<BR>Elvis Presley<P>Ok, those are just off the top of my head, but I've heard they were all "reportedly" gay.  It seems like the more famous they were, the more people are interested in proving they were gay.  Either they were or they weren't.  Who cares?  <P>It's silly enough to debate whether a living celebrity is gay/straight/bi, but a dead one?  Makes no sense to me.  ||||reg||1
