Z||000009||TRiAD||08-17-2001||09:56 AM||||One thing to keep in mind, gay rights activists (some of the extreme ones...every movement has them) will try to "out" someone they think the public likes after their death for a couple of reasons...<P>1) to surround the public with the thought that "everyone is gay"<BR>2) to bring in some people who'll say "well, if HE was gay, then it must not be..."<P>Many movements do this, try to bring in members from the "rich and famous" set when they're not around to deny or support it. <P>I'm not denying James Dean, if there are several sources with the same info, he may have well been, but just because you hear "so-n-so may have been gay", don't hang your hat on it and spread the "rumor". If you're really interested...look it up, or try to find out from multiple sources. <P>||||reg||1
